/**
 * General-knowledge records (Phase 3) — the single validated content
 * source for general knowledge.
 *
 * The records below were generated by script from the pre-move exports
 * of this module and ./answers.ts (the unit fields read from
 * docs/scaling/general-knowledge/items.json by the old adapter, which
 * never edited that data file). Content bytes come from those inputs
 * only: do not hand-edit a record here, and do not retype one. The
 * records are verified by the frozen-fixture test against
 * __fixtures__/main-7c04e3a7.json, captured from the old exports.
 *
 * Each record is one SubjectItem: the UnitItem fields (contract I2)
 * plus its answer, provenance, media rules and lead policy. Screens
 * read projections of these records (generalKnowledgeUnits,
 * answerFor); they never join files by hand. Provenance is
 * UNVERIFIED for all 10 records: no verifiedOn date exists for
 * these rows. Media is empty for all 10: general knowledge carries
 * no clip or still ids today. Lead policy is answer-not-in-lead
 * for every record.
 *
 * The opera-years-ago record is the one computed case: its play-time
 * answer is built per year by operaYearsEntry (./answers.ts) from
 * OPERA_OPENED_YEAR and is never stored. The record's answer is the
 * generator's output at the lint system's pinned year (2091) — the
 * specimen of the answer's shape, at the same year lint:subjects
 * evaluates the item.
 *
 * The slice keeps every row whose why / objective yields one
 * unambiguous multiple-choice answer with the shared AnswerCard
 * (v2: the 7-10 band grows from 3 to 5 items; 10-18 keeps its 3 and
 * 18+ its 2, as every row in those bands already played). One 7-10
 * row stays out: noon-shadow's objective is comparing three pictures
 * of a shadow, which needs a scene the shared flow does not have.
 * Every item was re-screened against the content rules: landmarks
 * appear as architecture and places only, balanced across
 * traditions, with settled facts only.
 *
 * The curated rows stay JSON-backed: docs/scaling/general-knowledge/
 * items.json holds 17 rows and the rows outside the live slice are
 * not records yet, so allGeneralKnowledgeRows() keeps reading the
 * data file (which this module never edits). rounds.json is PROPOSED
 * example rounds only — it is not read here.
 */
